WEBVTT

01:40.120 --> 01:44.700
We were really busy with our end of year cleaning and shopping, but...

01:44.700 --> 01:46.660
We can finally relax, right?

01:47.140 --> 01:50.000
The toshikoshi soba's almost done.

01:47.140 --> 01:50.000
[Note: Toshikoshi soba is eaten at the end of the year for good luck.]

01:50.000 --> 01:54.380
Oh, please stir the black beans for me, otherwise they'll burn, okay?

01:54.380 --> 01:55.880
Yep. Yep.

01:55.880 --> 02:00.930
Delighted with the Seven Deities of Good Luck

02:01.280 --> 02:06.100
Wanya's worked really hard and has made us all kinds of Osechi dishes.

02:01.280 --> 02:06.100
[Note: Osechiare traditional Japanese New Year dishes. Each has a special meaning at New Year.]

02:06.100 --> 02:10.980
Looks like we'll be able to have a nice New Year - quiet and relaxed.

02:10.980 --> 02:11.820
Yep.

02:11.820 --> 02:16.460
As our house is a temple, I kind of feel that we should do more, but-

02:16.460 --> 02:19.390
It can't be helped. The head monk isn't here.

02:19.390 --> 02:21.870
We'll have to ask them to forgive us this time.

02:21.870 --> 02:25.850
I think we should strike the bell for New Year's Eve at least.

02:25.850 --> 02:28.990
It can't be helped. The head monk isn't here.

02:28.990 --> 02:31.830
We'll have to ask them to forgive-

02:31.830 --> 02:33.380
Happy New Year!

02:33.380 --> 02:37.130
Happy New Year!

02:34.550 --> 02:36.490
It's not the TV!

02:45.970 --> 02:49.980
Let's see... how many times have I struck...

02:49.980 --> 02:52.940
Five... six... seven...

02:50.640 --> 02:52.940
That back... could he be...

02:53.630 --> 02:57.900
Ah! Kanata, Miyu-san, it's been a while.

02:58.200 --> 02:59.610
It is<i> my dad.</i>

02:59.610 --> 03:01.180
When did you...

03:01.180 --> 03:02.900
Come back?

03:02.900 --> 03:04.580
Oh, just now.

03:04.860 --> 03:09.780
Since I'm the head monk, I figured I should at least strike the bell for New Year's Eve.

03:09.780 --> 03:14.290
Um... Well, I struck it, so that should be good enough.

03:14.720 --> 03:16.090
You're finished already?

03:16.090 --> 03:18.870
It's not the number of times you strike it, but the feeling you put into it.

03:18.870 --> 03:21.260
Huh? Where's Fuku-chan?

03:24.570 --> 03:26.140
What's wrong?

03:26.140 --> 03:27.140
What?

03:29.600 --> 03:31.610
Who's that?

03:31.610 --> 03:32.810
Fuku-chan!

03:40.270 --> 03:43.890
I was surprised, Fuku-chan. You disappeared so suddenly.

03:43.890 --> 03:47.200
I was really hungry.

03:50.120 --> 03:53.140
N-Not just the Osechi dishes, but the black beans as well?!

03:53.840 --> 03:56.190
Is he a friend of yours, Dad?

03:56.190 --> 03:57.840
Yes, he is.

03:57.840 --> 04:01.840
After I finished my training in Nepal, I returned to India.

04:02.350 --> 04:05.620
I met him while I was training there. His name is Fuku-chan.

04:05.620 --> 04:08.310
Nice to meet you.

04:13.480 --> 04:16.100
What's with his head?

04:16.100 --> 04:18.050
He looks just like Fukurokuju.

04:16.100 --> 04:18.050
[Note: Fukurokuju is the God of Happiness, Wealth and Long Life.]

04:18.050 --> 04:20.400
Is he human? Or is he an alien?

04:20.400 --> 04:22.030
He's an alien.

04:22.030 --> 04:25.990
He wasn't at all surprised when he met me or Ruu-chama.

04:25.990 --> 04:28.150
Hasn't your dad noticed?

04:28.150 --> 04:29.530
It seems that way.

04:29.530 --> 04:31.760
I wonder if he's the real Fukurokuju?

04:31.760 --> 04:33.620
What's a Fukurokuju?

04:33.620 --> 04:38.870
Fukurokuju's one of the Seven Deities of Good Luck. He's a very auspicious and welcome god.

04:38.870 --> 04:40.940
That person is a god?!

04:40.940 --> 04:45.490
Someone who eats the Osechi dishes I slaved over without asking?!

04:45.490 --> 04:47.430
H-He might just resemble him.

04:52.520 --> 04:56.230
Isn't Fuku-chan's smile just wonderful?

04:56.230 --> 05:00.750
Those who are angry, crying children... they all can't resist smiling.

05:00.750 --> 05:03.740
It's truly amazing. It's the result of great training.

05:03.740 --> 05:05.540
I wonder why...

05:05.540 --> 05:09.170
I feel like I could forgive anything if he smiles at me like that.

05:09.170 --> 05:12.340
Oh, Mononoke, you think so too, eh?

05:12.340 --> 05:13.440
Yup!

05:14.710 --> 05:15.910
He didn't!

05:17.220 --> 05:18.630
He's eating again!

05:18.630 --> 05:21.770
He's even eating the toshikoshi soba I made.

05:21.770 --> 05:24.000
I wanted to eat that soba...

05:24.000 --> 05:26.690
Stop eating, Fuku-chan.

05:26.690 --> 05:30.010
It's bad for your stomach to eat this late.

05:30.010 --> 05:32.370
That's not the problem!

05:32.370 --> 05:33.970
Thank you for the meal.

05:38.970 --> 05:43.320
Even though I want to yell at him, I can't help but smile.

05:45.980 --> 05:48.010
I'm so full.

05:48.010 --> 05:49.560
Good night.

05:49.560 --> 05:53.390
Don't fall asleep here.

05:53.390 --> 05:55.830
Your room's over here.

05:55.830 --> 05:57.290
Fuku-chan's room?

06:04.820 --> 06:08.360
Dad, how long is Fuku-chan staying with us?

06:08.360 --> 06:12.270
Well, two or three days. Maybe even a week.

06:13.350 --> 06:15.640
Please take good care of him.

06:15.640 --> 06:17.440
Well, good night.

06:20.560 --> 06:22.280
What are we going to do?

06:22.280 --> 06:24.640
The money we placed aside for food expenses won't be enough.

06:25.860 --> 06:29.860
But it is New Year's day, so maybe it's auspicious.

06:30.720 --> 06:31.980
You're right.

06:31.980 --> 06:36.830
For someone who looks exactly like Fukurokuju to visit us on New Year's day, it could be a blessing.

06:37.140 --> 06:39.410
D-Do you think so?

06:50.720 --> 06:53.180
It's totally not auspicious at all.

06:53.180 --> 06:56.140
I don't need a blessing.

07:04.900 --> 07:06.650
[Sign: New Year's Day]

07:15.290 --> 07:17.200
Coming... coming...

07:17.200 --> 07:18.900
Hurry up! Answer the door!

07:18.900 --> 07:20.150
What are you doing?!

07:20.150 --> 07:22.370
Did you oversleep on the first day of the year?!

07:21.000 --> 07:22.370
We've got to visit the shrine!

07:22.720 --> 07:24.380
Oh, right... Then...

07:25.340 --> 07:26.440
Come in.

07:26.440 --> 07:28.280
Please come in and wait for us.

07:28.280 --> 07:29.360
Sure.

07:37.150 --> 07:39.480
Hey, there was a weird person over there just then.

07:39.480 --> 07:41.940
Hello, everyone. Please come in.

07:42.250 --> 07:45.610
Miyu-san and Kanata-san are just getting ready.

07:45.610 --> 07:49.190
Well, I overslept as well.

07:59.730 --> 08:01.160
What's wrong?

08:03.760 --> 08:07.770
Everyone, happy new year.

08:11.720 --> 08:14.660
Happy new year.

08:14.660 --> 08:16.430
Happy new year.

08:16.790 --> 08:24.530
Um... er... this is someone we hired to pretend to be Fukurokuju. Isn't that right, Kanata?

08:24.530 --> 08:29.150
What? Oh, right. That's right. Since it's New Year's day, we figured it'd be auspicious.

08:29.150 --> 08:34.380
Really? Now that you mention it, he does have an auspicious face.

08:34.380 --> 08:41.210
At first, I thought he had a really weird head, but now that you mention Fukurokuju, I can see it.

08:41.210 --> 08:45.590
That's right. If he's supposed to be Fukurokuju, it's not odd at all.

08:45.590 --> 08:49.360
I know! Since he's here, I'm going to pray.

08:49.360 --> 08:50.330
Me too!

08:50.330 --> 08:51.460
Me too!

08:53.630 --> 08:57.050
W-Wasn't it a great idea to hire someone to dress up as Fukurokuju?

08:57.050 --> 08:58.760
Yeah, it really was.

09:01.310 --> 09:04.870
I'm holding hands with Fukurokuju-chan.

09:04.870 --> 09:07.120
Me too! Me too!

09:07.120 --> 09:08.770
Both of you are so uncultivated.

09:09.150 --> 09:11.170
Well, I guess I will too.

09:09.410 --> 09:13.820
I never imagined Fuku-chan would be this popular.

09:14.460 --> 09:17.950
I wonder if it's okay to have Fuku-chan walk around town like this.

09:25.180 --> 09:27.600
That surprised me... His head...

09:27.600 --> 09:29.610
But he's supposed to be Fukurokuju I guess.

09:29.610 --> 09:33.380
You're right. It's normal on New Year's day.

09:33.810 --> 09:36.650
Somehow, everyone seems to be accepting it.

09:36.650 --> 09:37.800
Yeah.

09:49.710 --> 09:53.570
Even though he's the head monk of a temple, he's gone to a shrine for his first visit of the new year.

09:53.570 --> 09:55.400
Don't worry about it.

09:56.350 --> 10:00.230
However, Fuku-chan is sure blending well into the background.

10:00.230 --> 10:02.360
I'm glad he visited us on New Year's day.

10:02.360 --> 10:03.080
Yeah.

10:14.710 --> 10:16.700
Yay! I've got "excellent luck."

10:16.700 --> 10:17.640
Me too!

10:17.640 --> 10:18.720
Me too!

10:18.720 --> 10:19.930
Yay!

10:20.780 --> 10:24.140
"Small Luck" isn't bad, right?

10:24.140 --> 10:25.140
Yeah...

10:36.280 --> 10:38.820
What are they doing?

10:38.820 --> 10:40.310
It looks fun!

10:40.310 --> 10:42.450
Maybe I'll dance too!

10:42.450 --> 10:44.240
Me too!

10:54.130 --> 10:56.910
Hey, do you want to dance too?

10:56.910 --> 10:58.630
Hey, look at that...

11:03.750 --> 11:05.410
He's floating!

11:05.410 --> 11:06.620
Look at his head!

11:06.620 --> 11:08.810
It's growing!

11:12.270 --> 11:13.510
Let's go.

11:13.510 --> 11:14.650
Ready, steady, go!

11:16.800 --> 11:17.650
What?

11:19.340 --> 11:20.940
Miyu-chan!

11:20.940 --> 11:22.110
Saionji-kun?!

11:24.160 --> 11:26.640
Wait for us!

11:26.640 --> 11:28.860
Fuku-chan, wait!

11:41.970 --> 11:44.910
I wanted to dance some more with Fuku-chan.

11:44.910 --> 11:46.020
Yup!

11:46.020 --> 11:49.140
Fuku-chan's old. It'd be bad if his blood pressure increased.

11:49.430 --> 11:53.630
How boring. We were having so much fun too.

11:53.630 --> 12:00.120
But, Dad, Fuku-chan's head and feet were all like this... and this...

12:00.120 --> 12:02.070
Oh, you're talking about his ability to float,

12:02.070 --> 12:03.730
and to make his head extend?

12:03.730 --> 12:05.050
You knew?

12:05.050 --> 12:07.590
It must be the result of all his training.

12:07.590 --> 12:09.410
How auspicious... How auspicious...

12:10.460 --> 12:11.660
Then we'll see you later.

12:11.660 --> 12:12.670
See you later.

12:13.830 --> 12:16.840
Oh, about Fuku-chan...

12:16.840 --> 12:19.400
Since Fukurokuju Fuku-chan is here,

12:19.400 --> 12:23.850
don't you think it'd be even more auspicious if all the other Deities of Good Luck were here too?

12:24.840 --> 12:28.010
But I guess having one is very auspicious already.

12:28.330 --> 12:29.400
Later!

12:29.400 --> 12:30.490
Bye!

12:30.490 --> 12:32.520
Bye, Fuku-chan!

12:33.490 --> 12:37.000
Really... the things Santa-kun says.

12:37.000 --> 12:42.190
That's right. One's trouble enough. If we had all the Deities of Good Luck gathered-

12:45.170 --> 12:46.500
What's wrong?

12:48.050 --> 12:49.330
H-H-Hote-

12:52.750 --> 12:55.030
It's Hotei.

12:52.750 --> 12:55.030
[Note: Hotei is the God of Abundance and Good Health.]

12:55.030 --> 12:57.310
Hote-chan, I've been waiting for you.

12:57.310 --> 13:01.460
Oh, Fuku-chan! I guess this was the right place after all!

13:01.460 --> 13:04.570
Is everyone here?

13:04.570 --> 13:06.410
Yeah. They're all inside.

13:06.410 --> 13:08.220
Everyone?!

13:12.410 --> 13:14.400
He looks just like Daikokuten.

13:12.410 --> 13:14.400
[Note: Daikokuten is the God of Wealth, Commerce, and Trade.]

13:14.400 --> 13:16.350
Here we go!

13:18.020 --> 13:19.320
It's Ebisu!

13:18.020 --> 13:19.320
[Note: Ebisu is the God of Merchants.]

13:26.320 --> 13:28.450
Benzaiten...

13:26.320 --> 13:28.450
[Note: Benzaiten is the Goddess of Knowledge, Art, Music, and Beauty.]

13:30.390 --> 13:30.910
Over there!

13:31.290 --> 13:34.410
As expected, it's Bishamonten.

13:31.290 --> 13:34.410
[Note: Bishamonten is the God of Warriors.]

13:38.340 --> 13:42.540
It's the Seven Deities of Good Luck. Just like Santa-kun said...

13:42.540 --> 13:44.800
They're all gathered here...

13:45.480 --> 13:47.430
Did they all train with you?

13:47.430 --> 13:50.890
Nope. Other than Fuku-chan, this is the first time I've seen any of them.

13:51.540 --> 13:54.270
But everyone looks so lucky here.

13:54.270 --> 14:00.520
But there's only... one... two... three... four... five... six of them here.

14:00.810 --> 14:01.480
What?

14:01.820 --> 14:05.120
That reminds me, where's Ju-chan?

14:01.820 --> 14:05.120
[Note: Juroujin is the God of Longevity.]

14:05.120 --> 14:10.320
He's... actually knowing him, he may be lost.

14:10.320 --> 14:12.080
Oh dear.

14:12.080 --> 14:15.710
I guess we'll have to stay here for a bit longer then.

14:15.710 --> 14:17.050
What?!

14:17.050 --> 14:19.710
Until Ju-chan arrives,

14:20.080 --> 14:22.170
please let us stay here.

14:22.640 --> 14:25.370
Sure... sure... do as you please.

14:26.070 --> 14:27.680
Happy new year.

14:28.130 --> 14:29.150
Mikan-san!

14:29.790 --> 14:31.970
Happy new year.

14:33.480 --> 14:34.970
Happy new year.

14:36.110 --> 14:37.640
It's been a while, Miyu-chan.

14:37.640 --> 14:39.380
Mizuki-san!

14:39.380 --> 14:41.860
Coming now of all times...

14:42.640 --> 14:43.570
Hey!

14:43.850 --> 14:46.590
Mikan-san, please don't go in.

14:43.910 --> 14:47.150
Kung hei fat choi, akemashite omedetou, heureuse année nouvelle...

14:46.590 --> 14:49.900
That's right. We've got guests visiting, and-

14:47.150 --> 14:49.900
A happy new year!

14:49.900 --> 14:52.030
Guests? You mean those people?

14:54.140 --> 14:58.810
The Seven Deities of Good Luck? Your guests fit the new year's theme perfectly, don't they?

14:58.810 --> 15:03.450
Y-Yup, we hired them especially for New Year's day.

15:03.450 --> 15:06.800
However, one's late, so it's the Six Deities of Good Luck instead.

15:06.800 --> 15:08.340
Oh, I see.

15:08.340 --> 15:10.820
Oh. It's very in with the New Year's theme.

15:10.820 --> 15:12.720
How auspicious! How auspicious!

15:13.120 --> 15:14.790
Would you care for a drink?

15:14.790 --> 15:15.340
Thank you.

15:15.340 --> 15:16.680
That's enough now.

15:17.010 --> 15:19.730
We're a little busy today, so...

15:19.730 --> 15:21.740
Maybe next time.

15:23.010 --> 15:25.080
They're acting weird.

15:25.080 --> 15:28.280
It's New Year, so I'm sure they're very busy.

15:28.280 --> 15:30.900
Ah! You're drinking too much!

15:31.720 --> 15:36.960
I've got the feeling that I just found a great story, but I can't remember what it is...

15:38.320 --> 15:39.200
Sister...

15:40.450 --> 15:41.690
I was so panicked...

15:41.690 --> 15:44.340
I can't take this anymore...

15:44.880 --> 15:48.880
Happy new year.

15:51.410 --> 15:57.100
Erm... they're our relatives. Since it's New Year's-

15:57.100 --> 16:03.270
Yes, I heard. Your relative, Mitarashi-san, informed me.

16:04.730 --> 16:07.930
They're all wonderful people.

16:07.930 --> 16:12.000
You have wonderful relatives.

16:12.000 --> 16:13.240
Erm... Thank you.

16:13.240 --> 16:14.490
Why?

16:14.490 --> 16:17.910
I get why Momoka-chan isn't surprised, but why isn't Hanakomachi surprised?

16:17.910 --> 16:21.830
It's true that they're unique people.

16:21.830 --> 16:27.750
But since they're Kanata-kun's relatives, they're potentially my future relatives too.

16:30.920 --> 16:37.390
Ah, mine and Kanata-kun's wedding! Oh dear... Oh dear...

16:37.390 --> 16:38.810
How embarrassing!

16:38.810 --> 16:40.830
What should I do? What should I do?

16:40.830 --> 16:41.980
Where should we hold the ceremony?

16:41.980 --> 16:42.810
And what about our honeymoon?

16:43.310 --> 16:47.910
Hanakomachi, would you like to accompany Momoka-chan, Ruu, and I to the shrine?

16:47.910 --> 16:49.530
Of course! I'll come with you.

16:50.010 --> 16:51.690
Have a safe trip!

16:51.690 --> 16:53.990
Take your time!

16:56.810 --> 16:58.280
I'm home...

16:59.770 --> 17:02.960
I've had to visit the shrine twice today...

17:02.960 --> 17:04.950
Welcome back.

17:04.950 --> 17:07.370
Thank you for your hard work, Kanata-san.

17:07.890 --> 17:09.570
What about the others?

17:09.570 --> 17:13.470
Yes, yes. Well, they're all doing whatever they want.

17:25.370 --> 17:31.070
That good for nothing dad! He comes back and brings strange friends with him!

17:31.070 --> 17:35.480
They look like the Deities of Good Luck, but they're not auspicious at all.

17:35.480 --> 17:37.320
They just look like them, don't you think?

17:37.320 --> 17:40.700
Why did they come here anyway?

17:40.700 --> 17:41.820
Who knows?

17:41.820 --> 17:43.700
How long are they staying for?

17:43.700 --> 17:45.130
I dunno.

17:45.130 --> 17:47.040
I'm going to nap in my room for a while.

17:47.040 --> 17:48.040
Me too.

17:48.410 --> 17:51.000
If something happens, wake us, okay, Wanya?

17:52.230 --> 17:55.320
Even if a dog walks, it'll run into a pole...

17:55.320 --> 17:55.760
Got it!

17:56.220 --> 17:57.940
A nail in rice bran...

17:57.940 --> 17:59.220
Mine!

17:59.220 --> 18:01.890
Oh, from Planet Otto?

18:01.890 --> 18:03.930
Oh, you know it?

18:03.930 --> 18:07.600
Yup. I travel to all sorts of places.

18:07.600 --> 18:10.210
Wow! Really?

18:10.210 --> 18:16.450
Actually, Ruu-chama and I were sucked through a dimensional distortion while we were out for a walk,

18:16.450 --> 18:18.460
so we can't get back home.

18:18.460 --> 18:23.060
I see. It's true that the Planet Otto is fairly far from here.

18:23.060 --> 18:23.910
Yeah.

18:25.160 --> 18:30.380
Now that you mention it, before we came here, I heard about a rescue team from Planet Otto.

18:30.730 --> 18:32.380
Really?!

18:32.380 --> 18:34.440
Yup. We heard it too. We heard it too.

18:34.440 --> 18:35.300
Me too.

18:36.700 --> 18:38.260
I heard it too.

18:38.560 --> 18:41.490
I'm positive that they're fairly close.

18:42.390 --> 18:43.990
Ruu-chama!

18:44.580 --> 18:46.730
I hope you can go home soon.

18:46.730 --> 18:49.730
Yes! Thank you.

18:50.770 --> 18:52.650
Oh, it's the phone.

18:58.430 --> 19:00.950
Hello? Yes.

19:00.950 --> 19:03.160
What? The police station?

19:08.500 --> 19:12.120
He got lost trying to get to Saionji.

19:12.970 --> 19:14.960
I'm lost.

19:15.530 --> 19:16.940
Are you Ju-chan?

19:17.640 --> 19:18.960
Yes.

19:20.540 --> 19:22.340
Ju-chan! We were waiting for you!

19:22.700 --> 19:24.620
We were worried about you!

19:24.620 --> 19:26.550
I'm so embarrassed.

19:26.550 --> 19:29.270
I'm sorry I kept you waiting.

19:29.270 --> 19:31.610
Well, well, I'm glad you're here now.

19:29.650 --> 19:32.140
Now the Seven Deities of Good Luck are all together.

19:32.140 --> 19:32.810
Yeah.

19:53.790 --> 19:57.360
Okay, everyone, it's time to leave!

19:57.360 --> 19:59.800
Okay!

19:59.800 --> 20:01.720
Wh-What?

20:05.480 --> 20:09.520
No matter how you look at it, isn't this a sightseeing tour group?

20:09.520 --> 20:10.450
Yes!

20:10.450 --> 20:15.860
We're part of the Space Senior Citizens Club's Earth Sightseeing Tour.

20:16.190 --> 20:23.070
Thank you for allowing us to use Saionjii as our meeting point.

20:23.470 --> 20:25.090
Space Senior Citizens Club?

20:25.090 --> 20:26.530
Meeting point?

20:26.530 --> 20:30.990
Yes, our enjoyable Earth tour is over today.

20:30.990 --> 20:33.940
No one has forgotten anything, right?

20:33.940 --> 20:35.060
Nope!

20:41.200 --> 20:44.550
Ah, the ship to pick us up is here.

20:47.480 --> 20:49.520
What? The Treasure Ship?

20:47.480 --> 20:49.520
[Note: The Seven Deities of Good Luck are often depicted on their ship, the Takarabune or Treasure Ship.]

21:03.270 --> 21:08.160
Saionji-sama, everyone else, thank you for taking care of us.

21:08.160 --> 21:12.740
Um... We weren't able to-

21:12.740 --> 21:15.870
We didn't realize you were here on a sightseeing tour of the Earth.

21:16.170 --> 21:18.470
No, no. It's absolutely fine.

21:18.470 --> 21:20.540
Give my regards to the monk.

21:20.540 --> 21:22.570
Ah, I'll go and call my dad.

21:22.570 --> 21:25.590
It's fine. He's fast asleep.

21:26.030 --> 21:30.100
But we'd like to thank you all.

21:30.100 --> 21:31.580
Right, everyone?

21:32.670 --> 21:34.560
Please wait a moment.

21:34.560 --> 21:37.210
We don't need anything as a thank you.

21:37.210 --> 21:38.630
I wonder what it is?

21:38.630 --> 21:43.090
Who knows? But since it's something the Seven Deities of Good Luck are giving us

21:43.090 --> 21:44.820
maybe it's something auspicous?

21:44.820 --> 21:48.990
I'm sure it is! It could even be some gold coins or some treasure box.

21:49.350 --> 21:51.970
Yes. I'm sure that's it.

21:53.210 --> 21:54.410
I can't wait.

21:54.770 --> 21:56.510
Ready, steady, go!

22:05.020 --> 22:07.460
Maybe this is all we get?

22:07.460 --> 22:09.210
Well, that's fine too.

22:09.210 --> 22:10.010
Yeah, you're right.

22:10.310 --> 22:13.630
Even just their smiles are auspicious.

22:26.320 --> 22:27.120
Oh!

22:27.570 --> 22:28.860
They left, eh?

22:29.210 --> 22:30.510
Dad!

22:30.510 --> 22:32.040
You saw that?

22:32.040 --> 22:33.620
Yup. Extremely clearly.

22:33.620 --> 22:37.040
So you knew that Fuku-chan was an alien?

22:38.050 --> 22:39.630
An alien.

22:39.630 --> 22:42.570
An alien because they're in space.

22:42.570 --> 22:45.840
Earthlings are aliens too.

22:45.840 --> 22:47.750
Lots of leftover letters.

22:48.270 --> 22:50.150
Never mind all that.

22:50.150 --> 22:55.490
It's not often that you get to see such auspicious smiles.

22:55.490 --> 22:57.180
I guess you're right.

22:57.180 --> 23:00.270
I need to train more.

23:00.560 --> 23:01.360
Bye!

23:01.360 --> 23:02.730
What? Already?

23:02.730 --> 23:03.480
Uncle!

23:03.480 --> 23:05.480
Bye bye.

23:07.470 --> 23:10.930
What an amazing group.

23:10.930 --> 23:16.540
But you know, Fuku-chan and the others may have actually been the Seven Deities of Good Luck.

24:29.940 --> 24:59.960
Next Episode

24:31.590 --> 24:34.120
At Saionji, we're going to burn all our New Year's decorations,

24:34.120 --> 24:35.870
grill mochi, and have a great time with everyone.

24:35.870 --> 24:37.240
It's called Dondoyaki.

24:37.240 --> 24:40.180
Yippee! Yippee! I'll grill some dangos!

24:40.180 --> 24:41.940
Santa-kun brought fireworks.

24:41.940 --> 24:43.350
Everyone's excited.

24:43.350 --> 24:46.450
Next time on Daa Daa Daa: Matching Kimonos with Miyu.

24:46.450 --> 24:48.160
What? I can't find my kimono!

24:48.160 --> 24:50.550
What should I do? Everyone will be dressed in kimonos!

24:50.550 --> 24:53.470
Ruu-chama, please help us!

24:54.010 --> 24:59.960
Matching Kimonos with Miyu.

24:54.660 --> 24:55.970
Huh? Where are we?
